triage: fix_tests: The rules make the first round of each hand the passing round, with the 6 trick rounds coming after it. After `rounds: 1` each player should therefore still hold 6 cards (dealt, then 2 passed and 2 received), which is exactly what the game showed: deck empty, every hand 6 cards, trick_number 0. The tests wrongly expect every hand to be empty after only one round.
rewriting the independent tests
step D: evaluating
triage: revise_rules: The game was built correctly, but the design needs 6 choice steps per round, over the limit of 4. The extra steps come from the passing choice plus four trick plays in seat order starting from a leader who changes. Against random seats the results are also lopsided, with seat 4 winning 21 games and seat 2 only 10.
sending the rules back to the designer
